745	## What an action is
746	
747	An action is a span of time on one clip. Over that span, the clip's properties move from whatever they were when the span began to the action's **end state**, along the action's curve.
748	
749	Actions take the place of keyframes. You don't set a value at each moment. You set what the clip ends at, and the span and the curve do the rest.
750	
751	Actions on one clip can't overlap, and you can't make one that runs past the clip's end. A later trim can leave an action running past the end, and only the part inside the clip plays. See [How edits move actions](/motion/how-edits-move-actions/).
